## Why

The readers build and the accepted Phase 2 student workbook used two different leaf orders, and the
student workbook (the printer file) still printed empty reader strips. The orchestrator default, for
Daniel's look at the Phase 6 proof, is ONE leaf order: the Phase 2 order that R32 pins. Leaf 1 holds
strip 1 and 2 of the read-along, leaf 2 holds strip 3 of the read-along and strip 1 of the
decodable, and leaf 3 holds strip 2 and 3 of the decodable; the back of each strip sits in the same
slot.

## Commits

1. `9de1220f` `feat(storytime-print): one leaf order and the reader pages in the student workbook
   (Phase 4 Green 4c)` (3 files, 174 insertions, 86 deletions):
   - `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/readers.ts`: the workbook leaves use the R32 order. The new
     export `storytimeReaderStripSides(week, o)` returns the two reader pages of each strip side,
     rendered by the one page renderer, in the leaf order. The new export
     `readerPageCss(profile)` holds the reader page style. The side label `data-page-pairs` is gone,
     because one leaf can now hold two different strip numbers and a single label would be false.
   - `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/student-book.ts`: each reader strip holds the pages of its
     strip side from `readers.ts` (no copy of the page HTML). Every attribute and style that R32,
     R40, and A2 read is unchanged: `data-part="reader-strip"`, `data-reader`, `data-strip`,
     `data-slot`, the 198 x 140 mm box, the slot top, the strip mark with the reader and the strip
     number and `(back)`, the cut line, and the perforation by page parity. The strip is a flex row
     of two 99 mm pages, so a reader side stays one A4 page.
   - `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/print-fonts.ts` (new): the Andika and Sarabun faces move from
     `student-book.ts` to one module that both documents import, so no import cycle forms between
     `student-book.ts` and `readers.ts`.
   No test file changed.
2. The plan and evidence commit of this run: `measure(plan): record Phase 4 Green 4c and Hand-off 4`
   (the plan rows, this log, and the six evidence files).

## Gate results

Each gate ran as one whole command in one foreground `heavy-run.sh` wrapper, on the code commit
`9de1220f`.

- GREEN_TEST_COMMAND: exit 0. `Tests 384 passed (384)` on 11 files. Log:
  `jr-green-6883bd7d-green.txt`.
- PROJECT_TESTS: exit 0. `Tests 548 passed (548)` on 22 files. Log:
  `jr-green-6883bd7d-project.txt`.
- PROJECT_LINT: exit 0, no eslint output. Log: `jr-green-6883bd7d-lint.txt`.
- PROJECT_CHECKS: exit 0, one accepted FAIL (`published` for st2/1) and a clean `tsc --noEmit`.
  Log: `jr-green-6883bd7d-checks.txt`.
- No lock-wait line. No exit 75 or 137. `pnpm-lock.yaml` stayed unchanged. No `pnpm` command ran.

Two problems came up on the way and were fixed before the gates:
- `student-book.ts` first imported `fontFaceCss` from `readers.ts`, which does not export it; the
  unit test caught it at once (`fontFaceCss is not a function`), and the faces moved to
  `print-fonts.ts`.
- The reader pages first stacked inside the strip (block flow), so the workbook grew from 14 to 20
  PDF pages and R31 failed. The `.reader-strip` flex rule fixes it; R31 and R40 then pass.

